{"id": "EUVD-2026-102845", "enisaUuid": "1bf6df20-1ce7-332a-9041-43a9b919f4b3", "description": "SGLang 0.5.10 through 0.5.22 contains a code injection vulnerability in _evaluate_filter() that allows remote attackers to execute Python code by escaping the eval() sandbox through re.search __globals__. Attackers can send a crafted filter expression to the unauthenticated /dumper/configure endpoint when DUMPER_SERVER_PORT is set, running code in the scheduler process on the next forward pass.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T11:41:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T13:52:52", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44188", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/debug_utils/dumper.py#L1309-L1320", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/debug_utils/dumper.py#L1380-L1401", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-0.5.10-through-0.5.22-code-injection-via-debug-dumper-filter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111391", "GHSA-vfgj-p7f7-r3v8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8ccc23a4-403d-384f-96e7-f55a7ac3a7e5", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0.5.10 \u22640.5.22"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "39965291-69c0-343f-822b-182482a6f598", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}